@tikvahethiopia

**What did the National Security Council say?**

__The National Security Council announced its review of the national, regional and global situation in its meeting on April 1, 2017.

It issued a lengthy statement after the meeting.

In this regard, the Council noted that it had raised various issues that needed attention in its review.

The first was: “It concerns entities that pursue the backward option of enforcing their will through force.” The Council said: “These entities are present in different areas and abroad, although their appearance is different.”

- They see their own environment as more vulnerable and vulnerable than others;

- They do not want to talk or discuss;

- They are characterized by conspiracy, entrapment, robbery, suppression, cruelty, illegal trade and enforcing their will through force alone.

“Occasionally, they try to destroy each other because they have a common goal, destruction,” it said.

"They use legal party cover for illegal activities; they use corrupt politicians who have resigned from office to carry out illegal political activities; they use some problems of good governance in religious institutions to exploit them for political purposes," he said.

"The second elements are busy sitting in various places, collaborating with enemies of Ethiopia at home and abroad, obstructing government work, increasing public anger and spreading false rumors," he said.

- They try to carry out their evil purposes by infiltrating social spaces, religious places, offices and commercial places;
- They hide goods; 
- They create supply shortages; 
- They restrict the circulation of foreign currency; 
- They engage in smuggling;
- They illegally transport people and equipment. 
- They deliberately work to make the people angry through corruption, nepotism and corrupt practices.

"The third wing is the one that leads the false propaganda," the council said:
- They use the regular and social media to disturb the peace of the people; 
- When they are defeated on the battlefield; When their plots fail; When they lose a government that falls in a struggle and violence; They are using their last option;
- They create false history; 
- They store false information;
- They spread terrorist rumors;
- The government is fabricating news," he said.

The council announced, "The work of political, administrative and security institutions in coordination with the people has prevented the goals of the destructive forces from being achieved, and their capabilities and aspirations have been rendered futile."

(The council's full statement is attached above)

____@tikvahethiopia__

**What does the "Tigray Regional State Inclusive Transitional Administration Mission Statement" signed by General Tadesse Werede upon assuming the presidency of the Tigray Regional State Administration say?**

__1. To complete the process of returning displaced citizens to their homes, which has already begun, and to implement it __#expeditiously__ in the remaining areas;

2. To complete the process of disarmament and reintegration of former combatants in accordance with the Pretoria Agreement as soon as possible;

3. To establish the rule of law in the region; To stop significant illegal activities that threaten public safety, peace and security; To carry out appropriate regulatory and law enforcement work for this;

4. To ensure that regular development activities, government and social services, as well as reconstruction activities are carried out;

5. To put an end to relations and activities that deviate from the constitutional and legal order, ____#national sovereignty____ and the Pretoria Agreement;

6. To prepare the region for democratic elections; To work towards creating a democratic environment in the region where civil and political rights are implemented, and which accommodates political pluralism;

7. To facilitate the participation of the people of the region, various segments of society and political actors ____#in the national consultation process____;

8. To ensure that the media and communication activities of the regional government strengthen the unity and good relations of the people of the country, and respect the law and the constitutional order;

When General Tadesse Werede assumed his duties as President of the Interim Administration, he pledged to fulfill the above-mentioned responsibilities diligently and faithfully and signed ____#___.

